==Catalan==
===Etymology 1===
{{wikipedia|lang=ca|Català salat}}
So called because the people are said to replace '''sa''' for '''la'''. The resemblance with the past participle of {{l|ca|salar|gloss=to salt}} is coincidental.

====Adjective====
{{ca-adj|fstem=salad}}

# Referring to dialectal use of articles with ''s'' as opposed to the usual ones with ''l''. These articles descend from Latin {{term|ipse|lang=la}} and its forms, rather than {{term|ille|lang=la}} which served as the base for articles in most Romance languages.
#: {{l|ca|el}} → {{l|ca|es}}, {{l|ca|so}}
#: {{l|ca|la}} → {{l|ca|sa}}
#: {{l|ca|l'}} → {{l|ca|s'}}
#: {{l|ca|els}} → {{l|ca|es}}, {{l|ca|sos}}
#: {{l|ca|les}} → {{l|ca|ses}}

